# Copy to `.env.local` to override. Vite exposes only VITE_-prefixed values.

# Where artwork uploads go. Leave this file out entirely and the app does the
# right thing in both environments.
#
#   unset        → same-origin. Production posts to /upload on the Worker that
#                  serves the app; development uses /api, which Vite proxies to
#                  the locally running Worker.
#   "off"        → no uploads at all; images are embedded in the entry instead,
#                  as they were before the asset host existed.
#   absolute URL → that host, if the asset API is ever served somewhere else.
#
# An empty value means same-origin, NOT "off": that is how the deployed app is
# served, and treating it as opt-out would silently degrade every upload.
# VITE_ASSET_ENDPOINT=off
